ed[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]hand-offs, monitor follow-ups, and executing gates are all covered.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]A real-pipeline canary proves hijack then Continue works end to [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]end, and concurrent or crashed hijacks converge to exactly one [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]operation and at most one successor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]14[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agent_hijack_dependability.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/agent_hijack_dependability.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1t2[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1t2/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core: eligibility decision v2, occupant selection, [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]stop_blocked ledger state[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_decision_v2[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_decision_v2: in sase-core, add the v2 eligibility facts/decision [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wires (separate schema constant 2; mode [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]immediate|latched|redirect|refused, code, message, next_action, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]redirect_op), the occupant-selection function, and the additive ledger [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fields plus the stop_blocked state and its events. Expose PyO3 bindings,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add thin Python wrappers, and move sase's sase-core-revision.txt pin.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keep the hijack capability stamp and read the model facts [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]runners actually write[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]meta_facts[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]meta_facts: fix D3 (runner_capabilities erased by directive extraction) [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with one shared RUNNER_BOOT_META_KEYS tuple, a runner-side re-stamp, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]an invariant test. Fix D4 (wrong model-fact keys, float-only booted_at, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor/gate classified from live rows or never-written keys) using [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]durable records and a fixture captured from a real runner meta.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Snapshot discovery that sees real linked-repo metadata[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]snapshot_inventory[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot_inventory: make hijack stop/release snapshot discovery accept [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dict-shaped LinkedRepoResolution entries and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]opened_linked_workspaces.json and opened_siblings.json markers by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sharing one repository inventory with the commit finalizer, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fixtures built from real launcher metadata.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One facts builder, occupant resolution, and `sase agent hijack[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]--explain`[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]facts_resolver[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_decision_v2, meta_facts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]facts_resolver: build one Python facts builder used by every hijack [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]caller (no hard-coded facts), resolve names, session names, and session [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]containers to the occupying member through the Rust occupant selection, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and switch the stop orchestrator to the v2 decision. Add `sase agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hijack -e/--explain NAME` and the additive -j envelope keys, plus a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]screenshot-shaped fixture test.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI ingress uses the backend decision: precise toasts, [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]container retargeting, redirects[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui_ingress[dim] · [dim][/dim]after facts_resolver[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui_ingress: replace agent_can_offer_hijack with an asynchronously [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cached backend decision for the selected row; gate ,k, its footer chip, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the kill modal's h on it; toast code + message + next action; run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]non-destructive redirects; mirror hijack_record onto collapsed session [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows; log refusal codes; add a TUI/backend parity test.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Transactional stop hardening and target-level dedup[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]stop_txn[dim] · [dim][/dim]after facts_resolver, snapshot_inventory[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]stop_txn: target-level dedup that returns the active operation, verified[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]intent persistence before any signal, pin restore on pre-signal abort, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stop_blocked custody plus bounded retry on partial stops, pidfd [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]signalling on Linux, stale-sweep reconciliation of abandoned [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requested/stopping records, and session promotion so a sessionless stop [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]can still Continue.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Real-pipeline hijack canary[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]canary[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui_ingress, stop_txn[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]canary: a fakey end-to-end test that launches through the normal [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pipeline (anonymous workflow, real bootstrap, real directive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]extraction), asserts the real loader row gets an immediate decision, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hijacks through the TUI's own submission path, asserts HIJACKED with the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]workspace held, runs Continue, and asserts the successor settles in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]same workspace.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Durable hijack latch at agent-turn hand-offs[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]latch_core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after canary[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]latch_core: latched ledger state and events in sase-core; the decision [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]returns latched for finalizing turns and staged hand-offs; a Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]latch store keyed by target; runner checkpoints at staged-handoff [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]adoption, run end (moot), and retry boundaries; a pre- and post-spawn [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]guard that the follow-up fallback chain cannot swallow; dead-owner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconciliation; a bounded wait with an explicit force-now path; CLI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]-c/--cancel and -n/--now; and the TUI pending overlay.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hijack WAITING, QUEUED, and booting turns that hold a numbered[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]workspace[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]waiter_branch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after canary[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]waiter_branch: allow WAITING/QUEUED/booting turns with a numbered claim [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](terminate the parked runner, or take the processless branch when it is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dead), cancel the turn's own wait marker while waiters of it stay [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parked, redirect claimless %wait turns to kill-and-edit with a reason, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and make Continue relaunch a turn that never reached its provider.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Latch hijacks behind executing gates[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]gate_routing[dim] · [dim][/dim]after latch_core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate_routing: a gate executing its selected option yields latched; [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]settle_gate_turn applies the latch after the commands settle and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decision is recorded, suppresses and records the follow-up, and holds [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the workspace, never replaying or reinterpreting the decision. Continue [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launches the recorded follow-up.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor hijack adapter (closes the screenshot case)[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]monitor_adapter[dim] · [dim][/dim]after latch_core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor_adapter: running monitor turns become immediate through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stop_monitor with a hijack intent; the settlement funnel suppresses [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]--next, holds the workspace, and writes a hijacked done marker for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proc-backed and legacy monitors; a settled monitor with a pending [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-up latches. Recovery offers Continue (recorded follow-up with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]untrusted partial output), Escalate, Re-run command, View, Shell, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Dismiss.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Doctor check, resolving watchdog, and remote referral [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]tracking[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]ops_polish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after stop_txn, tui_ingress[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ops_polish: a `sase doctor` check for running agents lacking the hijack [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capability, a watchdog that reconciles resolving records whose successor[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]never dispatches, and local tracking of remote hijack referrals so the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mirror row shows the request until the owner host reports an outcome.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Boundary chaos test, crash convergence, and hand-off [/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]inventory guard[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]chaos[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate_routing, monitor_adapter, waiter_branch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chaos: a scripted fakey session (agent, sleep monitor, agent) that fires[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hijack at every checkpoint and requires HIJACKED, latched, or a defined [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]redirect, never a generic refusal; crash-between-steps convergence [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests; and a static guard test that fails when a new successor-launch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path lacks a latch checkpoint.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs sweep, glossary strand, and final verification[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]land[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chaos, ops_polish[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]land: reconcile the hijack Reference docs with the final behavior, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update the Agent Hijack glossary strand per the glossary_strand [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decision, run the final check, and record deferred follow-ups.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1t2","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bea